    "media:imagetext": "#7\nSunday.\nIn the meantime I am working on a lot of reports and proposals\nrequested by the Chinese officials with whom we are trying to deal. If\npatience 1s a virtue, we are among the most virtuous alive.\nI'hursday,\nNovember 4th.\nRained hard all day. Low ceiling, no possi-\nbility of air raid. News from Shanghai very bad. Have been pounding\nterror ll day bern m Balls don to his secretary,\n\"Miss Ella go slow\nbecause I'm in a helluva hurry\". There 1s absolutely\nno chance of getting a\nrellable typist in Nanking - all the Embassy people\nare writing their own\nletters and those who know how to operate a type-\nwriter are fortunate.\nBond radioed over CMAC system this morning that he arrived at\nShanghai safely without incident.\nMr. Peck 1s having a farewell dinner for Mr. Holm tonight.\nFriday, November 5th.\nNice party last night with two ladies present -\noccurrence in Nanking these days.\nMr. and Mrs. Richie, No.1 for-\neigner in the Post Office, Mr. Holm, Mr.and Mrs.MeDaniel, a newspaper man\nand Ambassador Johnson.\nToday has been another rainy day with low\nceiling.\nHave been here a week with not a single air raid. Ordinarily\na week of rainy weather 1s hard to take, but here a bright sunny day is\nushered in with curses. Have to see one of the Secretaries of the Ministry\nof Finance tomorrow.\nTheir Administration building was bombed and while\nnot badly damaged, they are all afraid to go back and are now quartered\nin the Ministry of Railways building temporarily while a bomb proof air\nconditioned concrete underground office is being constructed next door\nto the American Embassy.\nSaturday, November 6th. Another low overcast rainy day.\nWhen we were\nto operate a regular airline, such stretches of weather were the\nbane of our existence.\nThis weather is all the more remarkable for\nthe fall is usually the only good weather season in this section of China.\nToday I was grateful for that low ceiling as I had to spend the morning\nin the Ministry of Railways Building, itself normally the target for\nbomb attacks located as it is on the main street with the $12,000,000\nMinistry of Communications Building just across the street but even more\nof a target now because shared by two other Ministries, Finance and\nIndustry.\nHowever, even with good weather I suspect Nanking 1s reasonably\nsafe from indiscriminate bombing until after the Nine Power Treaty con-\nversations are concluded.\nWe do hear persistent rumors that the Capital\nwill be \"leveled to the ground\". These rumors have been especially current\nduring the last few days.\nSunday, November 7th. Another gray day with solid overcast at 2000 feet -\na disappointing talk with high Chinese official. The Chinese, as has been\nrightly said,\nare traders - not merchants. They are where they are because\nthey will not look far enough ahead.\nSincerely,",
